What is Polyhydroxybutyrate-valerate (PHBV)?
PHBV is a biodegradable thermoplastic polyester synthesized through bacterial fermentation processes. Composed of 3-hydroxybutyric acid (HB) and 3-hydroxypentanoic acid (HV) monomers, it exhibits excellent biocompatibility, mechanical strength, and processing versatility. Unlike conventional plastics, PHBV decomposes into carbon dioxide and water via microbial action, making it a sustainable alternative for industries transitioning toward circular economy models.
With properties comparable to polypropylene, PHBV finds applications across:
•	Medical materials (sutures, implants, drug delivery systems)
•	Packaging solutions (food containers, films, coatings)
•	Agricultural films (biodegradable mulches)
•	Consumer goods (disposable cutlery, 3D printing filaments)
